// Fictional, personal examples and a guided product tour. Never shared visitor data.
const DEMO_VERSION=3;
const DEMO_STORIES=[
 ['Dear diary, plot twist.','You do not need a main-character life to keep a diary. You need a place for the group-chat lore, the cold coffee, and the episode you absolutely did not stop at.\n\nWelcome to Wispr Diary. Click these pages and write whatever actually happened.','Yes, it does videos.','Movie-night evidence, exhibit A. Press play below.\n\nThe clip is Big Buck Bunny, a Blender Foundation animation. In your book, this could be your friend’s terrible dance or the concert you waited all year for.','movie'],
 ['One episode. Allegedly.','We said one episode. We watched four. The noodles went cold and someone kept pausing to explain a theory nobody asked for.\n\nA completely ordinary evening. Exactly the kind I want to keep.','Favourite character energy.','Not every photo needs to be a sunset. Keep the character you love, your desk at 2 a.m., or the food you swore you would photograph before eating.','pikachu'],
 ['Too tired to type? Same.','Click the microphone, then use your Wispr Flow shortcut. Talk directly into the diary page. No polished speech required.\n\n“It was a weird day and I don’t know where to start” is a perfectly good start.','A voice note, for the plot.','Press play to hear a sample voice note. This demo is computer-narrated, not a real person’s recording.\n\nUse Photo / video / audio to keep your own recording here.','audio'],
 ['Sticky notes are the side quest.','The pages are for your diary. Sticky notes are for the things that need a little extra space.\n\nGrab a note and drag it across either page. Double-click its words to edit. Select it to change its colour, size or angle.','Proof I was there.','A movie ticket. A receipt. A scrap of paper. Use Paper bits to add one, then make it yours.\n\nThese examples are made-up keepsakes, ready for you to rearrange.','ticket'],
 ['Your cover. Your rules.','Call it “My very normal life” or “Do not read, Mum.” Add your name, a subtitle, and a cover photo.\n\nDesign cover opens the editor. Pick a style and a typeface. You can change your mind later.','More than one personality?','Give each one a book. Everyday diary. Anime watchlist. Travel chaos. Big ideas.\n\nMy books keeps them together, with categories for finding the right one.','desk'],
 ['You are not running out of pages.','Previous and Next turn the spread. The page picker jumps straight to a chapter. Add pages gives you two fresh ones.\n\nThere is no fixed page-count limit in the app. Available storage still matters.','Keep the good stuff.','Keep this day saves an entry in this book. The memory box holds loose thoughts for later.\n\nDownload a backup from My books. Account sync is available once the sign-in service is connected.','paper'],
 ['Coffee, and a small victory.','I finished the thing I had been avoiding. Then I made a coffee that was mostly an excuse to stop checking my inbox.\n\nI am keeping both achievements.','Tiny, but documented.','This is the kind of photo I actually take: a cup, a table, a brief feeling that things are under control.','coffee'],
 ['The group-chat debrief.','A twenty-minute call became two hours. We discussed one actual problem and eleven imaginary ones.\n\nNobody solved my life. Everybody made it feel less dramatic.','Something they said.','“You can just call. You don’t need an update.”\n\nSaving that sentence before I forget how much it helped.','note'],
 ['A highly serious watchlist.','We made a list of films, then spent so long choosing one that we nearly did not watch anything.\n\nDecision-making: zero stars. Company: five.','The sofa cinema.','Ticket price: bring snacks.\nDress code: absolutely not shoes.','movie'],
 ['My desk has entered its final form.','One laptop. Three cables that may or may not be necessary. A notebook full of ambitious headings.\n\nThe tiny Pikachu is supervising. Performance reviews remain unclear.','A little room for favourite things.','You do not have to make every memory look grown-up. Keep the things that make a place feel like yours.','pikachu'],
 ['I cooked. Technically.','The recipe said twenty minutes. It was an optimistic recipe.\n\nDinner looked nothing like the picture, but everyone went back for more. I am calling that a successful adaptation.','The real recipe.','One distracted cook. One very patient friend. Whatever was left in the fridge.','ticket'],
 ['A note on the way home.','I recorded this because I knew I would forget the details by dinner. The bus was late, the day was loud, and I was unexpectedly happy.\n\nSometimes your voice remembers the feeling better than a sentence does.','Sound like yourself.','This computer-narrated sample shows where a real voice recording could live. No one needs to put on a “diary voice.”','audio'],
 ['A completely unproductive afternoon.','We went out for one thing and came back with pastries, a new inside joke, and none of the thing.\n\nI would like to defend this use of our time.','A receipt for a good day.','Two coffees. One shared pastry. No useful errands completed.','coffee'],
 ['Today needed a sticky note.','Not a big revelation. Just a reminder that I did something difficult and did not immediately give myself credit for it.\n\nHere is the credit. In writing.','For future me.','You handled more than you think.\nTake the win.','note'],
 ['A new idea on old paper.','The idea arrived while I was waiting for the kettle. I wrote it down before the kettle could become an excuse to forget it.\n\nThe first draft is allowed to be ugly.','Keep the rough version.','A paper scrap can hold the beginning of something. It does not need to explain the whole thing yet.','paper'],
 ['Rain cancelled the plan.','We stayed in, put on a film, and ate the snacks that were supposed to be for the journey.\n\nSome cancelled plans have excellent replacement plans.','The backup plan won.','A little animation, a blanket, and nobody asking what time we should leave.','movie'],
 ['A very minor obsession.','I went looking for one reference image and ended up explaining Pokémon types to someone who had not asked.\n\nIn my defence, they seemed interested for at least the first minute.','No need to be cool here.','Your diary can contain fandoms, collections, tiny obsessions, and extremely specific opinions. That is part of the person.','pikachu'],
 ['The deadline and the noodles.','The work got done. The noodles got cold. We reheated them and celebrated as though we had planned it that way.\n\nTeamwork sometimes looks like someone remembering you need dinner.','A small thank-you.','For the person who stayed on the call until I pressed send.','desk'],
 ['Home, without a headline.','There is no news. Someone bought the wrong biscuits. The same chair still squeaks. I heard the familiar kitchen noise through the phone.\n\nThat was the whole reason I called.','Ordinary sounds count.','A voice recording can keep the laugh, the pause, and the background chaos that text leaves out.','audio'],
 ['A ticket I almost threw away.','It was already folded in my pocket when I remembered I could keep it.\n\nNot because the ticket matters. Because it takes me back to who I was with.','The little evidence.','Use a photo of the real ticket, or make a paper version here. You decide what belongs on the page.','ticket'],
 ['I missed a few days.','For a minute, that felt like a reason to stop. Then I opened a fresh page.\n\nA diary is not an attendance register. It is a place you can return to.','Welcome back, whenever.','One sentence counts. A picture counts. “Today was a lot” counts.','note'],
 ['An extremely niche happiness.','The first sip was good. The playlist found the right song. Nobody interrupted the last ten minutes of the episode.\n\nI am not asking the day for much more than that.','My actual camera roll.','Coffee, screenshots, friends making faces, and the occasional photo that is mostly my thumb.','coffee'],
 ['Things I want to do again.','Cook with friends. Start a film before midnight. Call home without waiting for news.\n\nKeep making room for the parts of life that do not look impressive on a calendar.','A note worth moving forward.','You can make a copy of a book from My books, or keep adding pages to this one. The story belongs to you.','paper'],
 ['How to make this yours.','Try changing the cover. Drag a note somewhere completely different. Add a picture you actually took.\n\nThe demo is a starting point, not homework. There is no correct layout.','Privacy, minus the pretend.','This copy is saved on your browser. A local profile is not a cloud backup.\n\nUse Download a backup while real account sync is being connected.','desk'],
 ['Your turn, main character.','The sample stops at fifty pages. Your book does not have to.\n\nStart with the least impressive thing that made you smile today. It is probably the right thing.','And then what happened?','Write it. Say it. Add a photo. Keep the voice note.\n\nThe next page can be a little less demo, and a little more you.','pikachu']
];
function createSampleBook(){
 const mk=(type,text,x,y,w,url='',color='#f8ed89',font=21)=>({id:crypto.randomUUID(),type,text,x,y,w,url,color,font,tilt:-3});
 const spreads=DEMO_STORIES.map((c,i)=>{
  const pieces=[];const kind=c[4];
  if(kind==='movie')pieces.push(mk('video','Movie night · Big Buck Bunny\nBlender Foundation · CC BY 3.0',55,43,37,'assets/movie-night.mp4','#ffffff',17));
  else if(kind==='audio')pieces.push(mk('audio','The “one episode” incident\nComputer-narrated demo',54,45,39,'assets/voice-note.wav','#e7d9f2',19));
  else if(kind==='pikachu')pieces.push(mk('photo','Desk supervisor. Zero qualifications.',58,43,30,'assets/pikachu.png','#fffdf7',20));
  else if(kind==='coffee'||kind==='desk')pieces.push(mk('photo',kind==='coffee'?'The coffee deserved its own page.':'Notes, tabs, and a plan. Sort of.',56,44,35,'assets/'+(kind==='coffee'?'coffee.jpg':'desk.jpg'),'#ffffff',19));
  else if(kind==='ticket')pieces.push(mk('ticket','SOFA CINEMA\nFRIDAY · 9:00 PM\nADMIT ONE + SNACKS',55,48,36,'','#efd3e9',25));
  else if(kind==='paper')pieces.push(mk('cardboard','AN IDEA I HAD\nWhat if I actually started?\nFirst step: write it down.',55,48,35,'','#cba77a',23));
  else pieces.push(mk('note','You handled more\nthan you think.',56,48,32,'','#f8ed89',25));
  if(i===0)pieces.push(mk('ticket','NO PERFECT DAYS\nREQUIRED.\nJust your actual life.',10,70,29,'','#efc2ee',22));
  else if(i%4===1)pieces.push(mk('tape','a small thing worth keeping',9,73,31,'','#d6c4ea',18));
  return{id:crypto.randomUUID(),heading:c[0],diary:{left:c[0]+'\n\n'+c[1],right:c[2]+'\n\n'+c[3]},pieces,entryId:null};
 });
 return{id:crypto.randomUUID(),sampleVersion:DEMO_VERSION,isSample:true,title:'Dear diary, plot twist.',subtitle:'An interactive guide to your actual life.',author:'OPEN ME. I HAVE LORE.',category:'Sample books',color:'#7953a5',coverImage:'',coverStyle:'minimal',coverFont:'serif',entries:[],spreads,activeSpread:0,draft:structuredClone(spreads[0]),updated:new Date().toISOString()};
}
